Z||000032||DrRodey||08-07-2001||09:55 AM||||Ok... so it sounds like most everyone wants this to happen on a saturday.. Works as long as it is late enough for me... now the only problem is where are we gonna hold it??   Seeing as i've only been in this state for about two months I don't know too much outside the Denver Metro... any sugestions from long timers would be appreciated as to a good place to go for a meeting and preferably dinner afterward (or before for that matter)  I know back in MN we held it at a few different placed one was a fifties style diner.. Great place for a meeting.. had the car atmosphere and Great food.  The other was one of the local Pontiac Dealerships after-hours.. Great for our weekly tech Sessions... Both of these are goood options but it would also be kinda nice to have something unique to the area.  If any of ya'll have any ideas of places let me know and i'll check into them.  Thanks.<P>Dan<P>------------------<BR>Hi... My names Dan, and i'm addicted to Fieros.<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTIBLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>'84 coupe T-Top<BR>AOL IM = drrodey<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.JPG">     <BR> <A HREF="http://geocities.com/dr_rodey" TARGET=_blank>WEB SITE</A>||||reg||1
